402},"excerpt":"A confessing person voluntarily waives part of his BCO 35-10 right against","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga48_2021__2019-10_2019-12.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["case without process","BCO 38-1 confession","statement of facts approval","deposition from office","investigative committee report","self-incrimination","teaching elder discipline","confession procedures"],"case_numbers":["2019-12"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"This case was joined with Case 2019-10 (Evans v. Arizona Presbytery) and decided together. RE Pitts and co-complainants challenged the same BCO 38-1 procedural errors in TE Evans's deposition, and the SJC sustained both complaints on the same grounds."}},{"id":"bco:35-10--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Grady v. Southwest Florida","year":2009,"disposition":"sustained_in_part","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:35-10--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.md:occ-ffc393d96ca9","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":72},"excerpt":"4. Relative to Specification 4, no regarding BCO 32-20 and 35-3, and yes regarding BCO 35-10, but the error was not materially prejudicial to the accused.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.md"},{"id":"bco:35-10--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.md:occ-2478cbc6b2bb","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":176},"excerpt":"4. Did Presbytery err in its judgment in application of BCO 35-3, 32-20 and 35-10? No as to BCO 35-3 and 32-20; Yes as to BCO 35-10, but the error did not materially prejudice the appellant.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.md"},{"id":"bco:35-10--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.md:occ-6e2a06a59524","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":199},"excerpt":"misapplied BCO 35-10 (and 32-13) regarding telephonic testimony.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-16.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["Appeal","Ministerial discipline","Presbyterial jurisdiction","Due process","Censure and suspension","Constitutional interpretation","Judicial procedure"],"standard_of_review":"factual_findings","review_standards":["factual_findings"],"case_numbers":["2007-16"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"A minister appealed convictions and indefinite suspension arising from conflict over Presbytery's direction that he resign. The SJC upheld all three convictions, finding two procedural errors nonprejudicial and rejecting the other preserved challenges. But Presbytery could not treat its authority to dissolve a pastoral relationship as authority to compel resignation on pain of discipline. The SJC therefore vacated the censure and dissolution of the call and remanded for reconsideration of censure; Grady's separate administrative suspension remained effective."}}],"history":[{"kind":"change","year":2021,"ga":48,"note":"The indexed BCO change record names 35-10.","url":"markdown/ga48_2021.md","status":"section named in extracted change metadata","id":"7af238c677446cb51b99"}]}
